<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fürth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fürth is a city in Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, adjoining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>. Long a market town with one of the largest Jewish communities in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, it grew into an industrial city in the nineteenth century. In December 1835 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-railway">Ludwig Railway</a> between Nuremberg and Fürth, the first German railway worked by steam, opened between the two cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/furth.jpg" alt="Fürth" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kamran Salimi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fuerther_Innenstadt_Mrz_2020.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
